course: dictionary
lesson: 15206
title: Half a circle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A semicircle is half of a circle. The word has two parts: semi means half, and circle is the round shape. So a semicircle is a half circle.
explain: «We sat in a semicircle on the carpet.» Here the children made a curved line, like half a circle. Semicircle can describe a shape, and it can also describe things arranged in that curve.
explain: In maths, a semicircle has two edges: a curved edge and a straight edge called the diameter. The diameter goes straight across the middle, through the centre of the circle.
fact: A semicircle is half a circle.
fact: Semi means half, so semicircle means half circle.
fact: A semicircle has one curved edge and one straight edge, the diameter.
fact: The area of a semicircle is half the area of a full circle: ½ × π × r².
fact: The perimeter of a semicircle is πr + 2r: half the circumference plus the diameter.
exercise: «We sat in a semicircle on the carpet.» What is a semicircle? | A long straight line | A shape with straight sides and four corners | A full circle with a dot in the middle | *Half a circle, cut along its middle
exercise: A protractor is a semicircle marked from 0° to 180°. What is the highest number on a protractor? | *180 | 360 | 100 | 90
exercise: Cut a circle in half straight across its middle. What shape do you get? | A square | *A semicircle | A rectangle | A triangle
test: «The rainbow made a semicircle across the sky.» What does semicircle mean here? | A straight line | *A curved arch, like half a circle | A full circle with no gaps | A square with rounded corners
test: Which edge of a semicircle is straight? | The curved edge | The centre point | The circumference | *The diameter
exam: Ali says the area of a semicircle is πr², the same as a full circle. What is correct? | No, it is a quarter of the circle | Yes, it is double the circle | Yes, the same as a circle | *No, it is half of that: ½ × π × r²
